<div class="space-y-12">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight lg:text-5xl mb-4">
            <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-400 via-orange-400 to-amber-400 animate-gradient-x">
                SCIM Provisioning
            </span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-400 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Let an organisation&rsquo;s directory &mdash; Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, OneLogin &mdash; create, update and
            deactivate your app&rsquo;s users.
        </p>
    </div>

    <section>
        <pre data-filename="Terminal"><code class="language-bash text-sm">soli generate auth    # SCIM provisions the auth scaffold's User
soli generate scim
soli db:migrate up</code></pre>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            SCIM 2.0 is the protocol directories speak for that. It completes
            <a href="/docs/security/saml" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">SAML</a> or <a href="/docs/security/oauth-client" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">OAuth</a> sign-in,
            which only cover signing in.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="generates" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">1</span>
            What it generates
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 mb-4">
            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300">
                    <tr><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">File</th><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">What it does</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10 text-gray-400">
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>app/controllers/scim_controller.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">The SCIM server, under <code>/scim/v2</code>: users</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>app/controllers/scim_groups_controller.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Groups and their members</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>app/models/scim_group.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>ScimGroup</code>, <code>ScimMembership</code>, and what a group gives (<code>SCIM_GROUP_ROLES</code>)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>app/middleware/scim_active.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Keeps deactivated accounts out (<code># order: 8</code>)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>db/migrations/…_add_scim_user_indexes.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Index on the users&rsquo; <code>scim_external_id</code>; the <code>scim_groups</code> and <code>scim_memberships</code> collections</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>config/routes.sl</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">The routes, and <code>skip_csrf("/scim/*")</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">No file of the auth scaffold is edited.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="setup" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">2</span>
            Setup
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Give the directory a bearer token of its own, 32 characters or more:</p>
        <pre data-filename=".env"><code class="language-bash text-sm">SCIM_TOKEN=&lt;token&gt;                       # one directory
SCIM_TOKENS=okta=&lt;token&gt;,entra=&lt;token&gt;   # several, each named</code></pre>
        <p class="text-gray-400 my-4">A shorter token is ignored, so a placeholder left in <code>.env</code> opens nothing. Then, in the directory&rsquo;s provisioning settings: base URL <code class="text-amber-300">APP_BASE_URL/scim/v2</code>, authentication by bearer token (&ldquo;HTTP Header&rdquo; in Okta, &ldquo;Secret Token&rdquo; in Entra), and <code>userName</code> mapped to the user&rsquo;s email.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="endpoints" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">3</span>
            Endpoints
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 mb-4">
            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300">
                    <tr><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">Route</th><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">What it does</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10 text-gray-400">
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>GET /scim/v2/ServiceProviderConfig</code>, <code>/ResourceTypes</code>, <code>/Schemas</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">What the server supports</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>GET /scim/v2/Users</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">List (<code>startIndex</code>, <code>count</code>, up to 100 a page), or find with <code>filter=userName eq "…"</code> / <code>externalId eq "…"</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>POST /scim/v2/Users</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Create &mdash; <code>409</code> (<code>uniqueness</code>) when the <code>userName</code> exists</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>GET /scim/v2/Users/:id</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Read</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>PUT /scim/v2/Users/:id</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Replace</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>PATCH /scim/v2/Users/:id</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Update &mdash; what directories use to deactivate</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>DELETE /scim/v2/Users/:id</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Remove the account</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>GET /scim/v2/Groups</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">List, or find with <code>filter=displayName eq "…"</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>POST /scim/v2/Groups</code>, <code>GET</code> / <code>PUT</code> / <code>PATCH</code> / <code>DELETE /scim/v2/Groups/:id</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4">Create, read, replace, change members or name, delete</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Responses are <code>application/scim+json</code>; errors use SCIM&rsquo;s error schema.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="mapping" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">4</span>
            How a directory&rsquo;s user maps to an account
        </h2>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-white/10 mb-4">
            <table class="w-full text-sm text-left">
                <thead class="bg-white/5 text-gray-300">
                    <tr><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">SCIM</th><th class="py-3 px-4 font-semibold">Account</th></tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/10 text-gray-400">
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>userName</code> (else the first of <code>emails</code>)</td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>email</code>, lowercased</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>active</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>deactivated_at</code> &mdash; <code>nil</code> while active</td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>externalId</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>scim_external_id</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>displayName</code>, <code>name.formatted</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>name</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>name.givenName</code>, <code>name.familyName</code></td><td class="py-3 px-4"><code>scim_given_name</code>, <code>scim_family_name</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">An account a directory creates is a <code>member</code>, confirmed, with no password (and <code>scim_provisioned_at</code> set): it signs in through SAML, OAuth or a magic link, or sets a password with a reset link. Its first <a href="/docs/security/saml" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">SAML</a> sign-in links it with <code>SAML_LINK_EXISTING</code> off when its <code>externalId</code> is the assertion&rsquo;s NameID, or, by email alone, with <code>SAML_LINK_DIRECTORY=on</code> (the directory and the identity provider are one organisation&rsquo;s) &mdash; and, if it still has no password then, makes it <code>sso_only</code>. Deactivating a user here (<code>active: false</code>) is what ends their open sessions and tokens: <code>sso_only</code> only closes the ways in that bypass the identity provider.</p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mt-6 mb-3">Which accounts a directory can touch</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Only the ones it provisioned. An administrator, an account that signed up here, and another directory&rsquo;s account (<code>SCIM_TOKENS</code> names each directory, and an account remembers which one made it in <code>scim_directory</code>) are not there for it: not listed, not found by a filter, <code>404</code> on a read, a <code>PUT</code>, a <code>PATCH</code> or a <code>DELETE</code>, and never put in a group. So a leaked or over-eager token cannot move an administrator&rsquo;s address and then reset its password, deactivate the app&rsquo;s own accounts, or reach across tenants.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">A directory that finds no user under a <code>userName</code> creates one, and gets a <code>409</code> if a local account already has that address. To let it take such an account under its management instead &mdash; the way Okta and Entra match an existing user &mdash; set <code>SCIM_ADOPT_EXISTING=on</code>. Adopting an account <strong class="text-white">revokes what it could sign in with</strong> (<code>User#revoke_credentials</code>: password, sessions, API tokens, passkeys, linked identities): whoever created it is not known to be the person the directory means. An administrator is never adopted.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">A write that cannot be saved &mdash; a <code>userName</code> that is another account&rsquo;s, an address the model refuses &mdash; answers <code>409</code> or <code>400</code>, never <code>200</code>: a directory that reads <code>200</code> records the change, a deactivation included, as made.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Past twenty requests without a valid bearer token from one address in five minutes, the next ones are answered <code>429</code>; a request with the right token is always served, so nobody can switch a directory&rsquo;s provisioning off from its address. A token in <code>SCIM_TOKENS</code> may contain <code>=</code> (the pair is cut at the first one). A value that is not a string &mdash; a number, a hash, an array where a name or an address goes &mdash; changes nothing (only <code>remove</code> clears a field), and a <code>PUT</code> whose <code>userName</code> is not a string answers <code>400</code>. The login address follows <code>userName</code>, or the work or primary entry of <code>emails</code> &mdash; never another entry.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">Both shapes of <code>PATCH</code> are understood: Okta&rsquo;s, with no path and the attributes in the value, and Entra&rsquo;s, with a path and &mdash; for <code>active</code> &mdash; the string <code>"False"</code>, including <code>emails[type eq "work"].value</code>.</p>
        <pre data-filename="PATCH /scim/v2/Users/:id"><code class="language-json text-sm">{"Operations": [{"op": "replace", "value": {"active": false}}]}                 // Okta
{"Operations": [{"op": "Replace", "path": "active", "value": "False"}]}          // Entra</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="deactivation" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">5</span>
            Deactivation
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4"><code>active: false</code> closes the user&rsquo;s sessions (their session version is bumped, their remember-me cookie forgotten), and from then on <code class="text-amber-300">app/middleware/scim_active.sl</code> treats any request of theirs as a guest&rsquo;s &mdash; whatever signed them in: a password, a provider, a link, an API token. Checking there rather than in each sign-in action covers them all. <code>active: true</code> restores the account; the sessions closed meanwhile stay closed.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4"><code>DELETE</code> removes the account, after revoking its credentials (a linked identity or an API token left behind would name an account that is gone). To keep what it owns, change <code>destroy</code> in the controller to deactivate instead &mdash; the comment there says how.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="groups" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">6</span>
            Groups
        </h2>
        <p class="text-gray-400 mb-4">The directory creates groups and moves users in and out of them. A group gives nothing by itself; the app says what it means, two ways:</p>
        <pre data-filename="Soli"><code class="language-soli text-sm"># In a policy or a controller: read them.
ScimGroup.names_for(user).includes?("Finance")

# Or map them to the account's role, in app/models/scim_group.sl:
const SCIM_GROUP_ROLES = {"Finance": "accountant", "Support": "agent"}</code></pre>
        <p class="text-gray-400 my-4">With the mapping, a user&rsquo;s <code>role</code> follows their groups: in several mapped groups, the last one listed in the mapping wins; in none, <code>member</code>.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-400 my-4">A group belongs to the directory that created it. With several directories (<code>SCIM_TOKENS=okta=…,entra=…</code>) each sees and changes its own groups only &mdash; another directory&rsquo;s group is a <code>404</code>, like another directory&rsquo;s user &mdash; and two directories may each have a group of the same name. A name in the mapping stands for that group in every directory; write <code>"okta/Finance"</code> to mean the one of the directory named <code>okta</code> only.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-400">
            <li><strong class="text-white">A directory never makes an administrator.</strong> <code>admin</code> is granted in the app: a mapping to it is ignored, and an account that is an administrator keeps its role whatever its groups say. A compromised or misconfigured directory cannot hand out the app&rsquo;s administration.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">What a group gave is taken back at once</strong> when a user leaves it, when it is renamed, or when it is deleted: the role is recomputed on every change.</li>
            <li>Member changes are understood in the three shapes directories send: <code>add</code> / <code>remove</code> on <code>members</code> with a list of values, <code>remove</code> on <code>members[value eq "&lt;id&gt;"]</code>, and <code>replace</code> on <code>members</code> for the whole list. A user the app does not know is skipped.</li>
            <li>A user resource lists its <code>groups</code>, read-only: membership is changed on the group.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 id="limits" class="flex items-center gap-3 text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-6 scroll-mt-20">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-amber-500/20 text-amber-400 text-sm border border-amber-500/30">7</span>
            Limits
        </h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-400">
            <li><strong class="text-white">No bulk, sorting, ETags or password change</strong>, and the filters are <code>userName eq</code> / <code>externalId eq</code> on users and <code>displayName eq</code> on groups &mdash; what directories send, not the whole filter grammar.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">One role per account</strong>, and groups do not nest: a group&rsquo;s members are users.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Tokens are static</strong>, read from the environment; rotate by listing the new one beside the old in <code>SCIM_TOKENS</code>, then removing the old.</li>
            <li>A directory&rsquo;s token only opens <code>/scim/v2</code>; it is not a user&rsquo;s <a href="/docs/security/authentication#api-tokens" class="text-amber-400 hover:text-amber-300">API token</a>, and neither is it.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
